-- title:
--   Deterministic APSP in $O(n^{2.99791})$ time on a word RAM
-- statement:
--   All-pairs shortest paths on directed graphs with integer weights and no negative cycles can be solved deterministically in time $O(n^{2.99791})$ on a word RAM with $O(\log n)$-bit words:
--
--   $$\mathrm{APSP}.\mathrm{SolvedInTime}(2.99791).$$
--
--   **The problem.** An instance of size $n$ is a directed graph on the vertices $0,\dots,n-1$ given by a partial weight function $w$: $w(i,j)\in\mathbb Z$ is the weight of the edge $i\to j$, or undefined if there is no such edge. Instances have no negative cycle: every closed path has total weight at least $0$. The input is the $n\times n$ $0/1$ adjacency matrix followed by the $n\times n$ weight matrix (with $0$ where there is no edge), both row by row. The output has two cells for every pair $(i,j)$: the flag $1$ followed by the distance $d(i,j)$ (the weight of a path from $i$ to $j$ that is at most the weight of every such path) if $j$ is reachable from $i$, and the flag $0$ otherwise.
--
--   **The machine and the time bound.** $Q.\mathrm{SolvedInTime}(r)$ means: for every $\kappa\in\mathbb N$ there are a program $P$ of the word RAM, a number $b$ and a function $T:\mathbb N\to\mathbb N$ with $T(n)=O(n^{r})$ (precisely, $T(n)^{\mathrm{den}\,r}\le K\,n^{\mathrm{num}\,r}$ for some $K$ and all $n\ge2$) such that on every instance of every size $n$ whose input numbers have absolute value at most $n^{\kappa}$, and for every word size $W\ge b\,(\lfloor\log_2 n\rfloor+1)$, the program halts within $T(n)$ steps, accepts, and leaves the correct output in the cells right after the input. The word RAM has nine instructions (write the constant $1$; add, subtract or multiply modulo $2^W$; load; store; jump if negative; accept; reject); there is no division, no shift, no bitwise operation and no randomness.
--
--   The bound improves the deterministic exponent $2.99942$ of Theorem 22 of Alman and Vassilevska Williams. The algorithm saves $\delta=143/68400$, so $3-\delta\approx2.9979094<2.99791$; the margin absorbs the polylogarithmic factors.
--
--   This is the library form of the campaign goal `TrulySubcubicAPSP.apsp_bound_299791`; the platform node `TrulySubcubicAPSP.sourceSpecificationTransport` carries it over to the campaign's own definitions.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `APSP` and `Problem.SolvedInTime` are those of the namespace `EndStatement` (the library file `EndStatement.lean`, on the platform the definition `TrulySubcubicAPSP_SourceSpecification`); the exponent is the rational numeral $2.99791$.
